WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
(pensive music)
(spoon sliding)

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.400
- [Narrator] Phish Food, Chunky Monkey,

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.630
these quirky flavors are
unmistakably Ben &amp; Jerry's.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.500
But what really sets the brand apart

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.640
is its activism despite being owned

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.310
by one of the largest food
companies in the world.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.350
- It's been really fascinating to see

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.170
that Ben &amp; Jerry's has
really held their ground.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.480
- [Narrator] Companies that take a stance

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.080
on social and political issues

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.390
are becoming more important to consumers.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.050
According to research by
the polling firm Ipsos,

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.800
60% of consumers said
they would be more likely

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.520
to consider a brand that's aligned

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:32.910
with their own views.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.980
So how does the company blend activism

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.420
into its business model?

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.383
This is The Economics of Ben &amp; Jerry's.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.230
- Ben &amp; Jerry's really takes
a fairly liberal stance

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.670
on a lot of political issues.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.280
And Ben &amp; Jerry's has not shied away

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.500
from making those positions very public.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.770
- [Narrator] The company's social mission

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.110
is rooted in the values
of its two founders,

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:57.370
and their life experience
having grown up in the 1960s.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.890
- What's going on is genocide.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:02.020
- [Narrator] Ben Cohen and
Jerry Greenfield founded

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:05.110
the company in Burlington,
Vermont in 1978.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:08.260
Two years later, they were
selling pints to grocery stores.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.740
And in the late '80s, they
began using their ice cream

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.460
to support social causes.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.160
- They've spoken out about
how they were advised

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.100
by counterparts in the industry

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.830
that speaking out and taking
these activist positions

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.210
would hurt their bottom line.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.720
This was just not something

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.090
that businesses were doing.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:26.810
- [Narrator] But Ben
&amp; Jerry's pushed ahead

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:31.810
and by 1999, it reported
$237 million in sales.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.770
Today, the company says
the overwhelming majority

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.270
of its sales comes from
selling packaged ice cream

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:39.490
in supermarkets and convenience stores.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.680
- What the company has
shown over the years

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:44.910
is that if your product is delicious,

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:48.600
is attractive in other ways to consumers,

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.080
you can do these things

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.490
and still be a successful business.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:54.290
- Hi.
- Thanks so much.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:55.830
- [Narrator] Ben &amp; Jerry's
centered its business

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.320
on an idea it calls linked prosperity,

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.230
which means that has the company profits,

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.350
its communities should too.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.260
So when Ben &amp; Jerry's needed investors

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:07.510
to build its first
manufacturing facility in 1984,

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:10.720
it offered stock exclusively
to Vermont residents first

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.570
as a way to give back to the community

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.140
where it got its start.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:17.180
A year later, the Ben &amp;
Jerry's Foundation was born.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:21.480
It received 7.5% of the
company's annual pre-tax profits

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.200
to fund community-oriented projects.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.550
In 2000, multinational
food conglomerate Unilever

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:30.940
bought Ben &amp; Jerry's for $326 million

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.310
but the ice cream maker negotiated a deal

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:34.220
where it could maintain

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.790
its own independent board of directors.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:39.520
- While Unilever has made statements

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.720
over the years saying

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.920
that these are not the
issues of the whole company,

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.420
they have not been able
to stop Ben &amp; Jerry's

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:48.490
from making statements on social media

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:49.700
that get a lot of attention

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.560
because of how controversial they are.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.070
- [Narrator] After the killing
of George Floyd in 2020,

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:56.280
many companies started
posting on Instagram

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.960
to show their support for the
Black Lives Matter movement.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.470
While Ben &amp; Jerry's
released this statement,

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.330
saying "We must dismantle
white supremacy."

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:06.600
- They were so much more
direct than other companies

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.040
and that's where Ben &amp; Jerry's

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.810
has continued to be different.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.100
Because they've been
doing this for decades,

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.520
they have that credibility.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:16.980
- We need to have people
sitting in at their Congress,

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.490
people's offices, at
their senators' offices

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:23.010
and telling 'em we ain't leaving

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.764
'til you pass a Green New Deal.

00:03:25.764 --> 00:03:26.597
(people cheering)

00:03:26.597 --> 00:03:27.630
- [Narrator] But these bold statements

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.340
haven't been without backlash.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:32.470
For example, in 2021,
Ben &amp; Jerry's announced

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:34.120
that it would stop selling its products

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.100
in Jewish settlements in the
Israeli-occupied West Bank

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.120
and contested east Jerusalem.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.640
This decision was criticized
by Jewish communities

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.044
around the world.

00:03:43.044 --> 00:03:45.378
- And I will give up on my Ben &amp; Jerry

00:03:45.378 --> 00:03:47.930
and everything that Unilever produces.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:50.250
- [Narrator] And by Israeli politicians.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.890
Two months later, several state funds sold

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.540
or threatened to sell their
investments in Unilever

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.940
accusing the company
of breaking state laws

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:00.180
that prohibit the boycott of Israel.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.930
Unilever didn't respond
to requests for comment.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:06.220
At the time, the company declined
to discuss the divestments

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.130
but reiterated its commitment to Israel.

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:11.090
In February, Ben &amp; Jerry's posted

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:13.950
this tweet criticizing
President Biden's decision

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.900
to send US troops to Ukraine.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.970
- Unilever CEO said Ben &amp; Jerry's needs

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.490
to stay in their lane basically

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.730
and said that they should
not speak out about things

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.120
that they're not experts in.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.987
- [Narrator] A spokesman
from Ben &amp; Jerry's said,

00:04:25.987 --> 00:04:28.810
"We don't believe one must
be a foreign policy expert

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.400
to promote the ideals of peace

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.880
and to oppose armed conflict

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.150
as a solution to solve problems."

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:35.350
(spoon banging)

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.300
In addition to its public statements,

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.280
the company's social justice initiatives

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:42.390
are also baked into every
aspect of it business model,

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:43.970
how the ice cream is made,

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:47.587
how it's packaged and how
it's served to consumers.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.420
- There you are. No problem.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.040
- Thank you, thank you very much.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.870
- [Narrator] For example,
the brownies that are used

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:53.400
in flavors like Half Baked come

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.850
from a bakery in New York

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:57.830
that hires people who face
barriers to employment.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.050
Ben &amp; Jerry's also uses milk and cream

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:01.800
from family-owned dairy farms,

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.370
and all of its flavors
are fair trade certified

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.860
which guarantees that
farmers who grow vanilla,

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.350
cocoa and coffee beans get a fair price

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.490
for their harvest.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:14.200
- There's a flavor that's
gonna be supporting

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.210
the Poor People's Campaign.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.790
- [Narrator] For special edition flavors,

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.490
Ben &amp; Jerry's often works
with nonprofit organizations.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:21.970
- And a portion of the proceeds

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:26.030
will be donated to be
supporting the campaign.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:28.290
- So it's a real influence,

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:30.130
not just with consumers

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:32.560
but also by using their profits

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.410
to give back to these organizations.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:38.373
- Can I please have a Mint Chocolate.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:40.500
- [Narrator] Ben &amp; Jerry's also has

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:44.863
about 215 independently owned
scoop shops across the US.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.430
As corporate activism
becomes more important

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:51.750
to consumers, we might see more
companies voice their social

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.550
and political stances online.

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:57.100
So does this mean it's the end
of an era for Ben &amp; Jerry's?

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.867
A spokesman from the company says,

00:05:58.867 --> 00:06:01.280
"Ben &amp; Jerry's acts on
values it cares about

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:04.330
but trying to go at it solo
was never the intention."

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.913
(lively music)

